e global variable `g1` for atomicity violations following the <Read, Write, Read> pattern.\n\n**Operations on g1:**\n\nMain function (lower priority):\n- Line 29: `__VERIFIER_assert(g1 == 0)` - Read operation\n- Line 31: `__VERIFIER_assert(g1 == 0)` - Read operation  \n- Line 35: `__VERIFIER_assert(g1 == 0)` - Read operation\n\nISR (higher priority):\n- Line 9: `int tmp1 = g1 + 1` - Read operation\n- Line 10: `g1 = tmp1` - Write operation\n- Line 13: `int tmp2 = g1 - 1` - Read operation\n- Line 14: `g1 = tmp2` - Write operation\n\n**Analysis for <Read, Write, Read> patterns:**\n\nThe main function has consecutive read operations on `g1` that can be interrupted by the ISR's write operations:\n\n1. **Lines 29 → 31**: Consecutive reads in main\n   - ISR can interrupt and write at line 10: <29, 10, 31>\n   - ISR can interrupt and write at line 14: <29, 14, 31>\n\n2. **Lines 31 → 35**: Consecutive reads in main\n   - ISR can interrupt and write at line 10: <31, 10, 35>\n   - ISR can interrupt and write at line 14: <31, 14, 35>\n\nAll operations are accessible (no control conditions or interrupt disabling), so all violations are valid.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 10, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 14, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 10, 35]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 14, 35]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
